  "sections": [
    {
      "sectionId": "intro",
      "heading": "DnD 5e Feats: Character Optimization Guides for DnD 5e",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-intro-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "While feats are technically an optional rule, few groups play without them as they offer an additional way to add some mechanical fun to a character. If your group is using feats, you’ll typically select a feat in place of taking an Ability Score Increase."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-intro-2",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The feats listed below are usually covered in an article which addresses multiple feats because it is often helpful to consider on feat in the context of other, similar options."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-intro-3",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The list below is not comprehensive. For the full list and the text of each feat, please see "
            },
            {
              "type": "link",
              "text": "DnDBeyond",
              "href": "https://dndbeyond.com/feats"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
